# .projects.local.md — Private Projects Registry

Copy this file to `.projects.local.md` in your repo root. It is gitignored — your project names and paths never leak into the upstream repo.

When this file exists, AI agents read it alongside `AGENTS.md` as the authoritative project registry for this workspace.

---

## Projects Registry (Private)

`<root>` below is your workspace repo root (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`). Project folders live in its `projects/` subdirectory, so a Notes Path is `<root>/projects/<name>/`. If your repo is itself named `projects`, that is `.../projects/projects/<name>/` — keep both levels; never collapse to `<root>/<name>/`.

| Project | Collection | Notes Path |
|---------|-----------|------------|
| my-app | my-app | `<root>/projects/my-app/` |
| my-client | my-client | `<root>/projects/my-client/` |
| side-project | side-project | `<root>/projects/side-project/` |

**Repositories:** Each project's associated repos are listed in `<root>/projects/<name>/repos.json`. The panel reads this file to show git status per repo.

## Project-Specific Rules

Add any project-specific agent behavior overrides here, for example:

### my-client
- Uses yarn (not npm or pnpm)
- Never commit CLAUDE.md (gitignored in that repo)
